      "message": "Checking this guard at the earliest point of interaction seems good, which should be Device, but I could see putting it in DrawContext instead to make sure our internal usage doesn\u0027t go off thread either.\n\nSince the Device has a Recorder, though, wdyt about having a helper validateThreadOwnership() or something on recorder that Device can use w/o needing to hold on to SingleOwner? On the other hand, ResourceProvider doesn\u0027t hold on to the Recorder, so such a validate function wouldn\u0027t always be available it might be best to just pass the SingleOwner to everywhere that needs it.",
